# Site-wide security headers.
#
# Referrer-Policy is the important one: share tokens travel in the URL query
# (?t=, ?deck=<id>&token=, ?collection=<uuid>&token=). strict-origin-when-cross-
# origin stops the full URL (with token) from leaking in the Referer header to
# third parties on outbound navigations (TCGPlayer affiliate links, the YouTube
# embed, the QR image service). frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options stop the
# authenticated, mutating UI from being clickjacked inside a hostile iframe.
#
# NOTE: a full script-restricting Content-Security-Policy is deliberately NOT
# ENFORCED here yet — the app is a single no-build Index.html with inline module
# scripts and inline styles, so script-src still needs 'unsafe-inline'. But now
# that the core libs are VENDORED same-origin (see Index.html /vendor/*), most of
# script-src collapses to 'self', so a meaningful policy is finally worth shipping.
#
# A ready-to-enable enforcing policy is staged below (commented). The _headers
# file does NOT take effect on the local dev server, so it can ONLY be verified on
# a Netlify Deploy Preview. To roll it out safely:
#   1. On a deploy preview, add it FIRST as `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`
#      and exercise every surface (sign-in, scanner, deck poster export, graded
#      view, SC zip search, youtube embed) with the console open.
#   2. Add any origin that reports a violation (the lists below are best-effort).
#   3. Once clean, rename the header to `Content-Security-Policy` to enforce.
# Origins below were enumerated from Index.html + sw.js (2026-06-27 audit):
#   script:  self (vendored libs) + sentry loader + cdnjs (artist-poster html2canvas)
#            + 'wasm-unsafe-eval' (scanner onnxruntime-web WASM)
#   style:   self + Google Fonts CSS;  font: self + gstatic
#   img:     self + data:/blob: (LOGO_B64, canvas exports) + lorcast/tcgplayer/
#            qrserver/ravensburger.cloud/ebay/google-photo CDNs
#   connect: self + supabase (https+wss) + zippopotam + ravensburgerplay + sentry ingest
#   frame:   youtube embeds;  worker: self + blob: (scanner + canvas workers)
#
#   Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://js.sentry-cdn.com https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://cards.lorcast.io https://tcgplayer-cdn.tcgplayer.com https://api.qrserver.com https://ravensburger.cloud https://*.ebayimg.com https://lh3.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' https://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co wss://umwqowkiatjjltologrd.supabase.co https://api.zippopotam.us https://tcg.ravensburgerplay.com https://api.ravensburgerplay.com https://tcgcsv.com https://*.ingest.sentry.io https://*.sentry.io; frame-src https://www.youtube.com https://youtu.be; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
#
# The line below is the currently-ENFORCED policy (framing/object/base only),
# which is safe to ship standalone (it only restricts framing, not script exec).
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(self)
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Long-cache + permissive CORS on proxied Lorcast art.
#
# Lorcast (cards.lorcast.io) sends no Cache-Control header, so without an
# override Netlify edge treats the response as uncacheable — every miss
# forwards to Lorcast and pulls bandwidth across both legs of the proxy.
# A 30-day immutable cache lets Netlify's CDN absorb almost the entire
# load: each edge POP fetches once, then serves locally for a month.
# Image URLs are content-addressed (Lorcast appends a hash query param when
# they re-publish), so a long cache won't trap stale art — a new card
# revision arrives at a new URL the catalog ETL picks up.
#
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * guarantees canvas exports (deck poster,
# card poster, mover-tile) stay untainted no matter what Lorcast does with
# their CORS headers later. The browser only enforces CORS on
# crossOrigin="anonymous" <img>s — same-origin requests ignore it — but
# pinning ACAO is free insurance.
/img-proxy/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
